"""analysis.py -- Conformational free-energy surface of the ACE-CYS-NME capped
dipeptide via well-tempered metadynamics in OpenMM, with an externally
reconstructed free-energy surface derived from the recorded CV trajectory
and the first-order WT estimator.

Pipeline:
 1. Load data/dipeptide.pdb with openmm.app.PDBFile.
 2. Build system with ForceField('amber/ff14SB.xml'), NoCutoff, HBonds, no
    center-of-mass removal.
 3. Langevin middle integrator, T=300 K, gamma=1 ps^-1, dt=2 fs,
    Reference platform, deterministic seed.
 4. Energy-minimize and thermalize.
 5. Define two CVs: phi_CYS (atoms 5,7,9,16) and psi_CYS (atoms 7,9,16,18) of
    the central cysteine residue.
 6. Drive WT-metadynamics: bias factor gamma=10, hill height h0=1.0 kJ/mol,
    sigma=10 deg per CV, deposition stride 1 ps (500 steps),
    target 30 ns production (hard cap 100 ns).
 7. Maintain an *external* hill log computed only in NumPy; never read
    openmm.Metadynamics.getFreeEnergy(), _totalBias, _selfBias,
    getTabulatedFunction, or getFunctionParameters.
 8. After the run, reconstruct FES on a (72,72) cell-centered grid spanning
    [-180,+180) deg with periodic Gaussian summation and the order-1 WT
    estimator F = -(gamma-1)/gamma * V_bias.
 9. Detect up to 5 minima; write fes_2d.npy, minima.csv, fes_plot.png,
    cv_definition.txt.

When OpenMM is not importable in the actor venv (and pip install fails
because the network is unreachable), the script writes clearly diagnostic
placeholder artifacts instead of fabricating a result.
"""

